    thinking: "**Confirming Initial Validation**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the initial validation, including linting with `tsc --noEmit`, has passed without any errors! The codebase is clean. Now, I\'m carefully strategizing the refactoring. The primary goal is to create a dedicated file for each component and subsequently break down these components into more manageable, smaller units.\n\n\n**Planning Component Extraction**\n\nI\'m now deep in planning the extraction of components. My immediate focus is on ensuring a meticulous preservation of all existing styling and functionality during this refactor. The initial strategy is to create a well-defined structure for each section, for example, the Hero section will reside in `/src/components/hero/`, while preserving all aspects. Zero deviations from the original code are the current priority.\n\n\n**Defining Hero Component Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the granular structure of the `HeroSection`. I\'ve isolated individual components like `HeroBackground`, `HeroTopNav`, `HeroSocialFollow`, `HeroSpecialtyDroplets`, `HeroSpecialtyCard`, `HeroSpecialtySection`, `HeroDecorativeDropletGrid`, `HeroTypography`, `HeroActionButtons`, and `HeroBannerContent`, which will compose the larger `HeroSection`. I\'m meticulously mapping the relationships between these smaller units.\n\n\n**Composing Sections Meticulously**\n\nI\'m making excellent progress on composing the major sections now! I\'ve architected `HeroSection.tsx`, ensuring clean composition with `HeroBackground`, `ShapePatternSvg`, `HeroTopNav`, `HeroSocialFollow`, `HeroSpecialtySection`, and `HeroBannerContent`. I\'ve also begun work on the next section: \"Our Products,\" and have defined the components `ProductCard`, `ProductStarRating`, `ProductsHeader`, and `OurProductsSection`. I\'ve also designed the data structure for these Product cards, to facilitate easy management.\n\n\n**Constructing Training Components**\n\nI\'m now in the process of building out the training-focused components. I\'ve defined `WhyTrainWithUs.tsx`, including all sub-components. I\'m also composing `TrainLikeChampionSection.tsx`, which incorporates an `AthletePhotoCard`, along with `TrainingFocusAreas` and `WhyTrainWithUs`. This is coming together well, and I\'m ensuring everything is modular and reusable.\n\n\n**Defining Newsletter Architecture**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in architecting the Newsletter section. I\'ve broken it down into individual components, including the decorative droplets, the form with success view, and the `NewsletterCard` itself. I\'m focusing on the component relationships now, ensuring clean composition within the `NewsletterSection` to guarantee everything works seamlessly.\n\n\n**Structuring Footer Components**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the components for the footer section! I have the top divider, the 4-column grid layout, and the copyright notice to implement. I\'m also creating an `Overlay` component that shares droplets with other components. This includes the `VerticalDroplet` component, `DropletSvgPattern`, and `ProductDropletsOverlay` with a new clear organization.\n\n\n"
